# Questions for the rerank experiment (evaluation/rerank). 60 cases, assembled
# from two existing sets -- none written for this experiment, so none can have
# been shaped by what the reranker happens to do.
#
# 50 from origin/exp-topk (evaluation/topk/questions.jsonl), unchanged including
# their ids: 14 people + 36 courses, the 27/73 split of the two namespaces'
# vector counts (4,105 and 10,948), stratified broad/narrow/noans. golden.jsonl
# was rejected for this: 60 of its 63 cases are people, against a corpus that is
# 73% courses.
#
# 10 from origin/exp-select-llm (evaluation/selectllm/cases.jsonl, stratum
# "blended"), re-idded both-blended-* and given namespace null. They are the only
# questions anywhere that need BOTH corpora in one query -- the path /chat
# actually takes and that CLAUDE.md records as unmeasurable today. They are a
# CONTROL, not a target: the shape is multi-hop and reranking cannot fix it.
#
# id scheme: {corpus}-{stratum}-{slug}. namespace null means search them all.
